WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.990
- [Narrator] Principles for Success.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.210
An ultra mini-series adventure

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.490
in 30 minutes and in eight episodes.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.913
Episode one, The Call to Adventure.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.160
Before we begin, let me
just establish the fact

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.020
that I don't know much relative
to what I need to know.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.840
Whatever success I've had in life

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.290
has more to do with my knowing how to deal

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.963
with my not knowing than anything I know.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.840
That I should be telling
other people what to do

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.380
sounds kind of presumptuous to me.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.740
But I'm going to do it because I believe

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.030
that the principles that
have made me successful

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.223
could help other achieve their own goals.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.806
I'm now at a stage in my own life

00:00:41.806 --> 00:00:44.540
in which it is much more important to me

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.080
to pass along what I've learned about how

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.540
to be successful than to
seek more success for myself.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.060
What you choose to do with
these principles is up to you.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.770
You have to be an independent
thinker because only you can

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:02.960
develop your own principles
based on your own values.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.440
This brings me to my first
and most fundamental principle

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.760
which is that you need to think

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.750
for yourself about what is true.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.250
So let's get started.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.000
Early on, I've discovered
I needed principles.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.470
Principles are smart
ways for handling things

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.870
that happen over and over
again in similar situations.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.720
There are principles for everything.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.400
From skiing, to parenting,
to cooking, and so on.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.230
I'm going to share some
of my most important

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.210
overarching life principles that influence

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.353
how we approach everything that we do.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.180
I didn't start out with principles,

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.383
I acquired them over a
lifetime of experiences.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.593
Mostly from making mistakes
and reflecting on them.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:52.680
My life principles are simple
but they're not complete.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.200
I still struggle to
make the best decisions

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.720
and I still make mistakes

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.720
and learn new principles all the time.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.273
This is the reality.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.630
At the beginning, I needed to escape

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:06.810
the conventions that surrounded me

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.660
which meant that I needed
to think for myself.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.870
Unless you want to have a life
that is directed by others,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.610
you need to decide for yourself what to do

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.830
and you need to have the courage to do it.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.040
But I didn't know that at first.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.480
I only learned that from
going on my adventure.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.400
Looking back on my own journey,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.040
I now see that time is like a river,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.241
that carries us forward
into encounters with reality

00:02:34.241 --> 00:02:37.160
that require us to make decisions.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.220
We can't stop our movement down this river

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.670
and we can't avoid the encounters.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.763
We can only approach them
in the best possible way.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.410
In your lifetime, you will
face millions of decisions.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.220
The quality of your decisions

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.880
will determine the quality of your life.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.500
Over the course of my lifetime,

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.620
the most valuable things I've learned

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:01.810
were the results of
mistakes I've reflected on

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.100
to help form principles so I wouldn't

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.000
make the same mistakes again.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.890
These principles took me from being

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.618
a very ordinary middle-class kid

00:03:09.618 --> 00:03:12.910
from Long Island to
becoming very successful

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.180
as judged by conventional measures.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.650
They also gave me the meaningful work

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:21.120
and meaningful relationships
that I value even more

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.620
than these conventional successes.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.630
People often ask me how I did it.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.442
I can assure you it wasn't because

00:03:27.442 --> 00:03:29.840
of my uniqueness as a person.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.342
It was the result of a unique approach

00:03:31.342 --> 00:03:34.423
to life I believe almost
anybody can adopt.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.240
It starts with embracing
reality and dealing with it.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.683
In episode two, I'll
explain what that means.

